 "design": "R6 the smallest dependence this design could have found.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 15:05 EDT). The paper reports that the margin interval\nexcludes one and the accuracy interval does not, and it never says what the study was able to detect. A\nnull result carries no information until a reader knows the power behind it, and the accuracy conclusion\nis a null result. Someone reading that the accuracy interval runs from 0.993 to 1.157 deserves to know\nwhether a true ratio of 1.05 would have shown up or sailed past unnoticed.\nThis run measures it. It sweeps the true ratio over 1.00, 1.03, 1.05, 1.08, 1.10, 1.15, 1.25 and 1.40 by\nsetting the compound-symmetric correlation to the value each ratio implies, at the item noise of the\naccuracy battery, with 4,000 replicates per cell. It reports the rate at which the recipe-clustered\ninterval excludes one, which is size at a ratio of exactly one and power above it, alongside coverage so\nthe two can be read together. The smallest ratio whose exclusion rate passes four fifths is the smallest\ndependence the accuracy battery could reliably have found. Seed 20260964 keeps the draws distinct.\n",
